{% doc %}
  blocks/_featured-pills-group.liquid

  A container for one panel of **Featured pills**: a flex box with a surface,
  a frame and a set of blocks inside it.

  ## Why the theme already has this block, and this one still exists

  It is `blocks/group.liquid`. Same snippet, same setting ids, same behaviour
  down to the alignment swap and what Fill means — `snippets/group.liquid` is
  the whole implementation and nothing is reimplemented here.

  What it changes is one line of schema: the list of blocks it accepts.

  A private block — one with a leading underscore — can only be added where a
  parent names it, and `@theme` does not reach one. So a **Checklist row**
  cannot go inside an ordinary Group, and a column of them beside a photograph
  is exactly the arrangement this section was drawn as. `blocks/group.liquid`
  already carries four `_product-bundle-*` types by hand for the same reason;
  adding four more of this section's to it would put them in the picker of
  every group in the theme, where there is nothing for them to belong to.

  So this is that block with this section's private types listed instead, and
  it is itself private. The cost is one file; the alternative is either a
  section whose panels cannot be laid out, or a general block that offers every
  store four types it can never use.

  ## It is also the card

  `blocks/card-content.liquid` adds three things to a group — a background with
  an opacity, a blur, and a text colour. The first two are the group's own
  settings already (`background_color` takes a gradient, `backdrop_blur` is on
  the snippet), so the only one missing was the third, and it is one setting.

  That is why there is no private card block beside this one: a panel on a
  photograph and a column of rows are the same box with different values in it.
{% enddoc %}

{%- capture children -%}
  {% content_for 'blocks' %}
{%- endcapture -%}

{%- comment -%}
  Declarations, not an attribute: `snippets/group.liquid` writes the element's
  one `style`, and a tag with two of them keeps the first and silently drops
  the rest. `styles` is the parameter that exists for exactly this.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- capture panel_style -%}
  {%- if block.settings.text_color != blank -%}color: {{ block.settings.text_color }};{%- endif -%}
{%- endcapture -%}

{% render 'group',
   children: children,
   settings: block.settings,
   extra_classes: 'featured-pills-group',
   styles: panel_style,
   shopify_attributes: block.shopify_attributes %}

{%- comment -%}
  Every setting below is a control a merchant reaches in the editor, and the
  schema is one element's styling surface: splitting it to get under Theme
  Check's count of 40 would split the thing the settings style.
{%- endcomment -%}
{% # theme-check-disable ExcessiveSettingsCount %}
